From dd0fa0db916d18c978db76037c3d8283b9a19bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:18:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js): dispatch events along the DOM Standard's event path

Dispatch ran an element's own listeners and then its parentNode's, so it had
no capture phase, never crossed a shadow root to its host, never went from the
document to the window, ignored once/passive/capture on element listeners, and
never retargeted event.target. A click inside a web component never reached
the page's own listeners.

Dispatch now builds the event path once (assigned slots, shadow roots for
composed events, the document, the window except for load), runs capture then
bubble, retargets target and relatedTarget for every listener, honours
passive, and hides closed trees from composedPath(). Every target shares one
listener store. DOMContentLoaded and a viewport scroll fire once at the
document and bubble to the window, instead of being fired at both.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
